{"title": "Greenhouse", "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:322px;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Greenhousemainentrance.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"The main entrance of the Greenhouse interior.\" src=\"/images/thumb/Greenhousemainentrance.jpg/320px-Greenhousemainentrance.jpg?46a773\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Greenhousemainentrance.jpg/480px-Greenhousemainentrance.jpg?46a773 1.5x, /images/thumb/Greenhousemainentrance.jpg/640px-Greenhousemainentrance.jpg?46a773 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a>  <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Greenhousemainentrance.jpg\" class=\"internal\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The main entrance of the Greenhouse interior.</div></div></div>\n<p>The <b>Greenhouse</b>  is a botanical garden themed interior that only spawns commonly on <a href=\"/wiki/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">Faith</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Spine\" title=\"Spine\">Spine</a>. This interior has a very rare chance to spawn on any moon.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Rooms\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Rooms</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Interior_Features\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Interior Features</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Hazards\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Hazards</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Secondary_Objectives\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Secondary Objectives</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Power_the_Towers\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Power the Towers</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Stabilise_the_Water_Pressure\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Stabilise the Water Pressure</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Burn_the_Blatodara\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Burn the Blatodara</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Rewards\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rewards</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Event:_Blatodara_Swarm\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Event: Blatodara Swarm</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Gallery\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Gallery</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Rooms\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Rooms\">&gt; Rooms</span></h2>\n<ul><li><b>Fields</b> - The majority of the interior is covered in fields of corn. Scrap can spawn in specific and usually more open tiles here.</li>\n<li><b>Secure Greenhouse</b> - A small greenhouse with a button next to it. Completing a <a class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" href=\"#&gt;_Secondary_Objectives\"><b>Secondary Objective</b></a> and pushing the button reveals a reward inside.</li>\n<li><b>Shipping Container</b> - An interactable shipping container that spawns in the <b>Fields</b>. The door to open it can be locked and the container can have scrap inside it.</li>\n<li><b>Gazebos</b> - Multiple Gazebos are scattered throughout the <b>Fields</b>. Scrap can spawn around or under them. The breaker box also spawns attached to one.</li>\n<li><b>Greenhouse</b> - The garden is a larger, interconnected structure that has various plants inside. Scrap can spawn here on the floor or on shelves.</li>\n<li><b>Plasma Apparatus</b> - A blue apparatus hooked up to a machine that powers the entire facility. It generates somewhere in the <b>Fields</b>, is conductive, weighs 31lbs, and is worth \u25ae95.</li></ul>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Interior_Features\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Interior_Features\">&gt; Interior Features</span></h2>\n<ul><li><b>Decontamination</b> - When the apparatus is pulled, an alert and countdown for \"decontamination\" will begin. Afterward, all the sprinklers found within the <b>Fields</b> will activate and begin to spray flames and turn left about 90 degrees. They rapidly deal 6 damage per hit to the player and this decontamination lasts for about 45 seconds. This burns the corn and causes the interior to become smoky with a foggy-like effect.</li></ul>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Hazards\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Hazards\">&gt; Hazards</span></h2>\n<ul><li><b>Sprinklers</b> - Starting at 12:00pm, the sprinkler system on the roof of the interior will begin to activate every three hours. A loud buzzer will be heard three times before activation, most of the lights will turn red, and acidic pesticide will begin to rain down for about 10 seconds. This quickly deals 3 damage per hit to the player and the player must find cover to avoid taking damage.</li></ul>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Secondary_Objectives\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Secondary_Objectives\">&gt; Secondary Objectives</span></h2>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:322px;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GreenhouseSecureGreenhouse.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img src=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseSecureGreenhouse.jpg/320px-GreenhouseSecureGreenhouse.jpg?85a858\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseSecureGreenhouse.jpg/480px-GreenhouseSecureGreenhouse.jpg?85a858 1.5x, /images/thumb/GreenhouseSecureGreenhouse.jpg/640px-GreenhouseSecureGreenhouse.jpg?85a858 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a>  <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GreenhouseSecureGreenhouse.jpg\" class=\"internal\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The Secure Greenhouse.</div></div></div><p>One of three unique objectives will randomly generate for players to complete for one of three valuable rewards that will spawn in the <b>Secure Greenhouse</b>.\n</p><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Power_the_Towers\">Power the Towers</span></h3>\n<p>If the sticky note next to the button to open the <b>Secure Greenhouse</b> says \"POWER\", players must find and turn on four towers in the <b>Fields</b>. A panel will be attached to each tower with several switches. Each switch turns off or on different switches in a specific pattern, but the pattern generated is random. Players must turn all the switches green and both a sound effect will play and the tower will begin to glow red if players are successful.\n</p><p>After players turn on all four towers, a sound effect will play and they can return to the <b>Secure Greenhouse</b> to open the door for their reward.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Stabilise_the_Water_Pressure\">Stabilise the Water Pressure</span></h3>\n<p>If the sticky note next to the button to open the <b>Secure Greenhouse</b> says \"PRESSURE\", players must find the water pressure in the <b>Greenhouse</b>. A discernable hum will play when players are nearby this tile and there will be several panels with a button on them to interact with.\n</p><p>Players must keep every panel above the first red line but below the second red line to stabilise the pressure. Each time players successfully get every panel to this threshold, the pressure will stabilize. The fastest way to do this is to find the two panels that decrease pressure at the quickest rate and keep them near the first red line to constantly push it back up to the correct threshold. Other panels must be adjusted as needed and discernable click sound effects will happen when each panel goes above or below a specific threshold.\n</p><p>Once players have stabilized the pressure enough, all the panels will settle at a specific pressure and a sound effect will play. Players can now return to the <b>Secure Greenhouse</b> and open the door for their reward.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Burn_the_Blatodara\">Burn the Blatodara</span></h3>\n<p>If the sticky note next to the button to open the <b>Secure Greenhouse</b> says \"KILL\", players must burn groups of Blatodara in the <b>Fields</b>. These bugs are incredibly loud and relatively easy to find. To kill the bugs, players must interact with them while holding a <b>Match</b> in their hand, which is scrap that also spawns in the <b>Fields</b>. A group of Blatodara can be interacted with five times each and players must use 15 matches in total. Alternatively, players can pull the <b>Plasma Apparatus</b> to cause <b>Decontamination</b> to burn every Blatodara.\n</p><p>Once at least 15 Blatodara are burned, players can return to the <b>Secure Greenhouse</b> and open the door for their reward.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rewards\">Rewards</span></h3>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"text-align: center;\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<caption style=\"white-space: nowrap;\">Greenhouse Secondary Rewards\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Scrap Name</th>\n<th>Image</th>\n<th>Conductive</th>\n<th>Weight (lbs)</th>\n<th>Base Value</th>\n<th>Minimum Value</th>\n<th>Minimum Solo Value</th>\n<th>Maximum Value</th>\n<th>Maximum Solo Value\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rotten gantronium flower</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Rotten_gantronium_flower.png\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Rotten gantronium flower.png\" src=\"/images/thumb/Rotten_gantronium_flower.png/60px-Rotten_gantronium_flower.png?dd7052\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"item-preview thumbborder\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Rotten_gantronium_flower.png/90px-Rotten_gantronium_flower.png?dd7052 1.5x, /images/thumb/Rotten_gantronium_flower.png/120px-Rotten_gantronium_flower.png?dd7052 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></div></div></td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>11</td>\n<td>160</td>\n<td>160</td>\n<td>187</td>\n<td>223</td>\n<td>260\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gantronium flower</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Gantronium_flower.png\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Gantronium flower.png\" src=\"/images/thumb/Gantronium_flower.png/60px-Gantronium_flower.png?f89cb6\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"item-preview thumbborder\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Gantronium_flower.png/90px-Gantronium_flower.png?f89cb6 1.5x, /images/thumb/Gantronium_flower.png/120px-Gantronium_flower.png?f89cb6 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></div></div></td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>11</td>\n<td>270</td>\n<td>270</td>\n<td>315</td>\n<td>377</td>\n<td>441\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Haltronium flower</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Haltronium_flower.png\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Haltronium flower.png\" src=\"/images/thumb/Haltronium_flower.png/60px-Haltronium_flower.png?d5f7bc\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"item-preview thumbborder\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Haltronium_flower.png/90px-Haltronium_flower.png?d5f7bc 1.5x, /images/thumb/Haltronium_flower.png/120px-Haltronium_flower.png?d5f7bc 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></div></div></td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>11</td>\n<td>420</td>\n<td>420</td>\n<td>491</td>\n<td>587</td>\n<td>686\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p>The reward is randomized, but the chance for a more valuable reward is increased by how early in the day players complete the objective and is influenced by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://lethal.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics#Furniture_luck\">the vanilla luck system</a>. The value of the reward is additionally increased by a difficulty multiplier, ranging from 0.6x to 1.4x, and a solo (singleplayer) multiplier of 1.17x. <b>Stabilise the Water Pressure</b> is considered Easy difficulty and has a 1.0x multiplier, <b>Power the Towers</b> is considered Medium difficulty and has a 1.15x multiplier, and <b>Burn the Blatodara</b> is considered Hard difficulty and has a 1.4x multiplier. The base value and multipliers for objective rewards can be adjusted in the Wesleys Interior Tools config under the Secondary Objectives section.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Event:_Blatodara_Swarm\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Event:_Blatodara_Swarm\">&gt; Event: Blatodara Swarm</span></h2>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:322px;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GreenhouseBlatodaraSwarm.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img src=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseBlatodaraSwarm.jpg/320px-GreenhouseBlatodaraSwarm.jpg?7ecbb8\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseBlatodaraSwarm.jpg/480px-GreenhouseBlatodaraSwarm.jpg?7ecbb8 1.5x, /images/thumb/GreenhouseBlatodaraSwarm.jpg/640px-GreenhouseBlatodaraSwarm.jpg?7ecbb8 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a>  <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GreenhouseBlatodaraSwarm.jpg\" class=\"internal\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The Blatodara Swarm.</div></div></div><p>A large gazebo with a hole and pot next to the hole can be found either in the <b>Fields</b> or adjacent to the main entrance. After interacting with and pushing the pot into the hole, the <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> will be angered, rise from the hole, and cause walls to rise up and trap players inside.\n</p><p>Players must enable the four acid sprayers in the corners of the arena. To do so, players must turn all the switches on the panel attached to the the sprayer green. Each switch turns off or on another switch in a specific pattern, but the pattern generated is random. If successful, the acid sprayer will turn on.\n</p><p>The <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> deals 8 damage per hit to players that come into contact with it. The <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> will additionally form arms and hands to attempt to hit players with four different attacks:\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Sweep</b> - The <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> will sweep a hand slowly around two sprinklers, dealing 8 damage per hit to players that come in contact with it.</li>\n<li><b>Spin</b> - The <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> will spin three arms around the arena in one direction before spinning them in the other direction, dealing 8 damage per hit to players that come into contact with them.</li>\n<li><b>Slam</b> - The <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> will repeatedly slam three of its hands to the ground and create small aftershocks, dealing 15 damage per hit to players that come into contact with either.</li>\n<li><b>Smack</b> - The <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> will smack one of the acid sprayer panels, resetting it and dealing 8 damage per hit to players. There currently might be a softlock where the <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> can attack an inactive acid sprayer and cause it to effectively be disabled the entire fight despite players still being able to turn it on.</li></ul>\n<p>A relatively safe way to avoid most attacks or avoid accumulating too much damage is to crouch in the corners of the arena. Players can also jump onto the acid sprayers and jump above attacks like the <b>Sweep</b> and <b>Spin</b>. An extension ladder can be repeatedly placed near a wall and climbed to avoid all attacks as well.\n</p><p>After players keep the sprayers on for long enough and keep turning them back on after the <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> disables them, the <b>Blatodara Swarm</b> will violently explode and scatter. Afterward, the <b>Blatodara commander</b> can be found on the ground. This is the reward for the event. It is not conductive, weighs 0lbs, and is worth \u25ae196 to \u25ae239.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Gallery\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Gallery\">&gt; Gallery</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GreenhouseFields2.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"The Fields.\"><img alt=\"The Fields.\" src=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseFields2.jpg/120px-GreenhouseFields2.jpg?37a4a9\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseFields2.jpg/180px-GreenhouseFields2.jpg?37a4a9 1.5x, /images/thumb/GreenhouseFields2.jpg/240px-GreenhouseFields2.jpg?37a4a9 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">The Fields.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GreenhouseShipping.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"A Shipping Container prompting players to unlock it.\"><img alt=\"A Shipping Container prompting players to unlock it.\" src=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseShipping.jpg/120px-GreenhouseShipping.jpg?5b4076\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseShipping.jpg/180px-GreenhouseShipping.jpg?5b4076 1.5x, /images/thumb/GreenhouseShipping.jpg/240px-GreenhouseShipping.jpg?5b4076 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A Shipping Container prompting players to unlock it.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GreenhouseGazebo.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"A Gazebo with a Breaker Box.\"><img alt=\"A Gazebo with a Breaker Box.\" src=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseGazebo.jpg/120px-GreenhouseGazebo.jpg?3b21a4\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseGazebo.jpg/180px-GreenhouseGazebo.jpg?3b21a4 1.5x, /images/thumb/GreenhouseGazebo.jpg/240px-GreenhouseGazebo.jpg?3b21a4 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A Gazebo with a Breaker Box.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GreenhouseGardenEntrance.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"An entrance to the Greenhouse.\"><img alt=\"An entrance to the Greenhouse.\" src=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseGardenEntrance.jpg/120px-GreenhouseGardenEntrance.jpg?c23ecc\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/GreenhouseGardenEntrance.jpg/180px-GreenhouseGardenEntrance.jpg?c23ecc 1.5x, /images/thumb/GreenhouseGardenEntrance.jpg/240px-GreenhouseGardenEntrance.jpg?c23ecc 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">An entrance to the Greenhouse.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a